{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\IonosGlobalNavigation\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "migration-name-length",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/Migration/Version000000Date20181013124731.php:45 index ionosglobalnavigation_user_id_index of ionosglobalnavigation: 35 characters, in Nextcloud 27"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 name in the migrations is longer than the server allows, so it stops the install or the update of the app with an exception. The table names are counted with the default prefix oc_.",
        "  Up to Nextcloud 32 the server checks this only where info.xml lists no database, or lists oci among them.",
        "  lib/Migration/Version000000Date20181013124731.php:45 index ionosglobalnavigation_user_id_index of ionosglobalnavigation: 35 characters, in Nextcloud 27"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "psalm/phar, phpunit/phpunit are in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
